-- Version 18: city outlines that match the real city limits (and Google Maps).
-- Udaipur used to be the Udaipur assembly constituency, a much bigger and differently shaped area that left
-- Lake Pichola and Fateh Sagar outside the "city". Kolkata was 141 old KMC wards from DataMeet and missed
-- the newer wards 142 to 144 around Joka.
-- Udaipur: the 70 wards of Udaipur Municipal Corporation, joined into one shape (about 60 sq km), from the
-- Swachh Bharat Mission urban ward maps (Government of India), via github.com/ramSeraph/indian_admin_boundaries.
-- Kolkata: the Kolkata Municipal Corporation boundary in OpenStreetMap (about 197 sq km), via Overture Maps.
-- Both simplified to about 15 m. Earlier migrations have already run on the live site; never edit them.
